winewayland, dcomp: show a window's child windows above its own swap chain; apply a window's constant layered alpha

Adobe Lightroom 9.6 (the cloud app, lab runtime 11.10-185): it launches signed in and its menus and toolbar draw, but
everything below the toolbar is one flat gray (28,28,28), 3/3. Its modal cards ("Get started", "Organize and edit
your photos locally") sit on an opaque black backdrop that hides the whole window.

Mechanism 1 (gray content area). Lightroom does not use DirectComposition (no DComp device is created). It presents one
D3D11 swap chain per content container (the content root, the grid container, the grid; each presented about once, at
startup and on resize, with the clear color only) and draws every panel, the grid, the empty-library prompt and both
toolbars as CHILD windows of those containers (WS_CLIPCHILDREN; GDI and ID2D1DCRenderTarget), some of them
WS_EX_LAYERED with LWA_ALPHA 255. Wine draws those children into the top-level's window surface; DXVK's Vulkan client
surface of the container is a subsurface above that surface and hid all of them (probe: the committed window surface
holds the left panel, 0x2d2d2d, where the screen shows 28 gray). Patch 150 (direct HWND chains) is not involved: its
kill switch changed nothing. A second gap kept even NEUTRON_DCOMP_SUPPRESS_CLIENT=1 from showing the UI until a resize:
the win32 z-order mirror (neutron_restack_apply, on by default with NEUTRON_OWNED_ZORDER) ignored place_below for the
surfaces its walk finds and lifted them straight back above the window surface.

Windows. A window's child windows are composed above the window's own swap chain; a WS_CLIPCHILDREN window's presents
never cover its children, and DWM keeps layered children above it. Upstream winex11 models this by rendering a window
with children offscreen and copying each present through the window's DC (needs_offscreen_rendering: "window has
children, needs compositing").

Fix 1. winewayland: a client surface whose window is registered with the dcomp bridge (__wine_dcomp_blit) and has
WS_CLIPCHILDREN and a visible, non-transparent child over its client area is placed below the window surface, and the
window is marked __wine_dcomp_below; the z-order mirror now honors place_below. dcomp: a chain made for its own window
(patch 150's direct case) is copied through the window's DC while that mark is set (the DC clips the children; checked
about every 100 ms, and the frame already on screen is copied at the switch, since Lightroom may not present again).
Windows without such children keep patch 150's direct path unchanged.

Mechanism 2 (black backdrop). The backdrop is a top-level WS_EX_LAYERED window with SetLayeredWindowAttributes
LWA_ALPHA 191. win32u creates its surface without the layered flag (only UpdateLayeredWindow sets it), so winewayland
used an XRGB buffer and never applied window_surface->alpha_bits: solid black (every pixel 0,0,0). Windows blends the
whole window at that alpha. Fix 2: a non-layered surface with an LWA_ALPHA constant below 255 gets an ARGB buffer with
the constant applied premultiplied (wl_shm ARGB8888 is premultiplied). Layered and blur-behind surfaces keep their paths.

Not covered: sibling windows overlapping a swap-chain window inside the same top-level (they stay under its client
surface); raw Vulkan/OpenGL windows with children (only DXGI chains registered with the bridge are copied); windows
without WS_CLIPCHILDREN; the copy costs a readback per present while children cover a chain (Lightroom presents
rarely). Seen once, not judged: one capture taken mid-switch from Edit to Export showed the old Edit panel half
replaced; 4 s later the Export view was whole. Separate item, not touched: the export folder picker's Open with an
empty name did nothing; typing the folder path worked.

Lab (11.10-185lc = 185 + x86_64 winewayland.so, x86_64 and i386 dcomp.dll from this patch; fresh reflinks of the
signed-in Lightroom prefix AcLr-1; desk at 175 %, 168 dpi):
  185 (adobe-ac-lr L1-L3, LrDc-1/2/3/6)   main view one color (28,28,28) 7/7; backdrop solid black
  185lc LrDc-7/8/9                        library view at startup 3/3 (left panel, "Add some photos", toolbars;
                                          53 colors); backdrop translucent 2/2 (UI behind at 25 %: 28 -> 7, 45 -> 11)
  185lc workflow LrDc-8/9 (n=2)           Local mode, Pictures\lrtest grid thumbnail, photo opened, Edit: Exposure +
                                          Shadows (photo mean 101.7 -> 232.0 both runs), Crop corner + Enter (Edit menu:
                                          "Undo Crop Rectangle"), Export (Shift+E) -> chepino-2.jpg 2048x1444 (source
                                          4886x3236: aspect 1.418 vs 1.51 = cropped), 2/2
  185lc + both kill switches LrDc-10/11   main view one color 2/2, backdrop black 2/2 (== 185)
  Regression on 185lc, n=1 each, the new rule never fired (0 neutron-children-copy lines): Photoshop 2026 Home, new
  document, text, restore/maximize (0 px Home, 0.05 % after resize vs 185rc); Premiere 2026 project, seek, Export
  Frame, text, restore/maximize (0 px vs 185rc but Home 1,915 px); Topaz Photo sign-in drawn (caption strip 0 px vs
  fonts2); CapCut settings menu + main window 2/3 == 185 numbers, 1/3 hung at startup in an ntdll loader-lock
  deadlock (peb_lock vs loader_section) before any present; ntdll is unchanged, INFERRED unrelated, base rate open.
Kill switches: NEUTRON_DCOMP_CHILDREN_COPY=0 (children over a chain; read by winewayland), NEUTRON_WINDOW_ALPHA=0
(constant layered alpha).

--- a/dlls/dcomp/device.c
+++ b/dlls/dcomp/device.c
@@ -135,8 +135,21 @@
     ID3D11Texture2D *staging; /* NEUTRON perf: cached staging texture, recreated only on size change */
     UINT   staging_w, staging_h;
     LONG   last_client_w, last_client_h; /* NEUTRON: pause blits while the target is mid-resize */
+    BOOL   hwnd_direct; /* NEUTRON: a chain made for this very window (patch 150): copied only while children
+                         * sit over it (neutron_children_over_chain) */
